ecord ID obtained from listing records or another API call - this tool cannot search or list records. Use the list records tool to find record IDs. Empty field values are not returned in the response.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["baseId", "tableIdOrName", "recordId"], "properties": {"baseId": {"type": "string", "examples": ["appXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"], "description": "ID of the Airtable base."}, "recordId": {"type": "string", "examples": ["rec4YsVV8cU6V4EiT", "recGoHq5YJGaUJX24"], "description": "ID of the record to retrieve. Must be a real record ID obtained from listing records or another API call. Format: starts with 'rec' followed by exactly 14 alphanumeric characters (e.g., 'rec4YsVV8cU6V4EiT'). This tool retrieves a single specific record - to list or search multiple records, use the list records tool instead."}, "timeZone": {"type": "string", "examples": ["America/New_York", "Europe/London", "UTC"], "description": "Time zone for formatting dates when cellFormat='string'. Required when cellFormat='string'. Uses IANA time zone format (e.g., 'America/New_York', 'Europe/London', 'UTC')."}, "cellFormat": {"enum": ["json", "string"], "type": "string", "default": "json", "examples": ["json", "string"], "description": "Controls cell value formatting: 'json' for native types, 'string' for all values as strings. When 'string', timeZone and userLocale are required."}, "userLocale": {"type": "string", "examples": ["en-us", "en-gb", "de-de"], "description": "User locale for formatting dates when cellFormat='string'. Required when cellFormat='string'. Uses BCP 47 language tag format (e.g., 'en-us', 'en-gb', 'de-de')."}, "tableIdOrName": {"type": "string", "examples": ["tblXXXXXXXXXXXXXX", "Marketing Leads"], "description": "ID or name of the table."}, "returnFieldsByFieldId": {"type": "boolean", "default": false, "description": "If true, field keys in the response are field IDs; otherwise, field names."}}}, "hasFullSchema": true}, "AIRTABLE_LIST_RECORDS": {"toolkit": "AIRTABLE", "tool_slug": "AIRTABLE_LIST_RECORDS", "description": "Tool to list records from an Airtable table with filtering, sorting, and pagination. Use when you need to retrieve multiple records from a table with optional query parameters.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["baseId", "tableIdOrName"], "properties": {"sort": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["field"], "properties": {"field": {"type": "string", "description": "The name or ID of the field to sort by. Must be an actual field in your table - cannot use system metadata fields like 'createdTime', 'lastModifiedTime', or 'id'. Use AIRTABLE_GET_BASE_SCHEMA to discover available field names."}, "direction": {"enum": ["asc", "desc"], "type": "string", "default": "desc", "description": "The direction for sorting. Defaults to 'desc'."}}}, "description": "Array of sort objects to apply to records. Each object specifies a field and direction. Records are sorted by the first sort object, then by the second, and so on. IMPORTANT: Cannot sort by system metadata fields like 'createdTime' or 'lastModifiedTime' - these are metadata properties returned with records but not sortable fields. To sort by creation/modification time, you must add a 'Created time' or 'Last modified time' field to your table (using those field types in Airtable)."}, "view": {"type": "string", "examples": ["viwXXXXXXXXXXXXXX", "Grid view"], "description": "The name or ID of a view to use for filtering and sorting records. View names are case-sensitive. View IDs (format: 'viwXXXXXXXXXXXXXX') are more reliable than names and not affected by view renames. Use AIRTABLE_GET_BASE_SCHEMA to discover valid views. Note: this parameter is overridden if sort parameter is provided."}, "baseId": {"type": "string", "examples": ["appXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"], "description": "The ID of the Airtable base. Must start with 'app' followed by 14 characters."}, "fields": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "examples": [["fldABC123", "fldDEF456"], ["Name", "Status"]], "description": "Array of field names or IDs to include in the response. If not specified or if ['*'] is passed, all fields are returned. Field names are case-sensitive and must match exactly as they appear in Airtable. The Airtable API accepts both field names and field IDs interchangeably in this parameter, regardless of the returnFieldsByFieldId setting. IMPORTANT: System fields 'id' and 'createdTime' are always returned automatically as part of the record structure - do NOT include them in this parameter. Only specify user-defined table fields here. UNKNOWN_FIELD_NAME errors indicate: (1) a typo or case mismatch, (2) the field was renamed/deleted, or (3) you included a system field name. RECOMMENDED: Use field IDs (format: 'fldXXXXXXXXXXXXXX') for reliable operation. Use AIRTABLE_GET_BASE_SCHEMA to retrieve valid field names and IDs."}, "offset": {"type": "string", "description": "Opaque pagination cursor token returned in the 'offset' field of a previous list records response. This value must be used exactly as returned by Airtable - do not construct, modify, or decode it. IMPORTANT: Do not pass numeric values like '50' or '100' - these are not valid offsets. Offset tokens are complex opaque strings generated by Airtable. Only pass an offset if you received it from a previous response's 'offset' field. Omit this parameter for the first page of results."}, "pageSize": {"type": "integer", "default": 100, "maximum": 100, "minimum": 1, "description": "Number of records to return per page. Must be between 1 and 100. Defaults to 100."}, "timeZone": {"enum": ["utc", "client", "Africa/Abidjan", "Africa/Accra", "Africa/Addis_Ababa", "Africa/Algiers", "Africa/Asmara", "Africa/Bamako", "Africa/Bangui", "Africa/Banjul", "Africa/Bissau", "Africa/Blantyre", "Africa/Brazzaville", "Africa/Bujumbura", "Africa/Cairo", "Africa/Casablanca", "Africa/Ceuta", "Africa/Conakry", "Africa/Dakar", "Africa/Dar_es_Salaam", "Africa/Djibout