{"data": {"results": [{"index": 1, "use_case": "Extract structured product details from this webpage into JSON.", "execution_guidance": "IMPORTANT: Follow the recommended plan below. Extract steps before execution, adapt to your current context, execute sequentially with current_step parameter, and check known pitfalls to avoid errors.", "recommended_plan_steps": ["[Required] [Prerequisite]: Define required fields and strict JSON contract using FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT (schema/prompt as the output spec).", "[Required] [Step]: Fetch the page using FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE (markdown and/or HTML) and validate the body is substantial content (not a placeholder/interstitial) and check embedded status/error fields.", "[Optional (if content is missing, dynamic, or overly trimmed)] [Step]: Re-run FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE with broader capture (onlyMainContent adjusted), a render delay (waitFor), and/or raw HTML to capture client-rendered sections.", "[Optional (if multiple related pages are needed)] [Step]: Enumerate candidate URLs using FIRECRAWL_MAP_MULTIPLE_URLS_BASED_ON_OPTIONS, then collect them via FIRECRAWL_BATCH_SCRAPE and retrieve results using FIRECRAWL_BATCH_SCRAPE_GET.", "[Required] [Step]: Produce structured fields using FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT (max 10 URLs per call) and retain any returned job identifier.", "[Optional (if extraction returns a job or partial output)] [Next Step]: Poll until complete and fetch final JSON using FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT_GET.", "[Fallback (if scraping returns an interstitial, needs multi-step interaction, or actions are brittle)] [Fallback]: Use FIRECRAWL_START_AGENT to navigate and return the same target content/fields, then (if needed) normalize to the schema with FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT or SCRAPFLY_EXTRACT_DATA."], "known_pitfalls": ["[FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT] Max 10 URLs per call; larger sets require chunking or batching upstream.", "[FIRECRAWL_EXTRACT_GET] Some runs are asynchronous; initial responses may be empty/partial until the job finishes.", "[FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE] Tool success may still return an interstitial/warning page; validate content, not only status_code.", "[FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE] Heavy pages can fail with 408 SCRAPE_TIMEOUT; retry with waitFor/broader capture or switch to FIRECRAWL_START_AGENT.", "[FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE] Response nesting varies and large markdown may truncate; markdown can be nested under multiple data objects, and metadata may indicate queueing/concurrency limiting."], "reference_workbench_snippets": [{"description": "Safely read markdown across common FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE response shapes", "code": "```python
